abstract: |
  DR-QFormer is a BLIP-2-style parameter-efficient middleware for 
  Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG). It uses learnable query tokens 
  in a Q-Former architecture to bridge frozen retrievers and frozen 
  large language models. The system trains only the Q-Former (~57M params) 
  and task-specific heads (~0-3M params) across three tasks:
  
  - Task E: Fragment-level Entailment Tagging (filtering)
  - Task S: Fragment-level Sorting Supervision (ranking)
  - Task C: Condensing-Generation with Contrastive NLL (knowledge extraction)
  
  All core components are fully implemented with 16/16 tests passing.
  Dual training (Primal QA + Dual QG) with shared parameters enforces
  bidirectional query-answer reasoning.
